   228	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   229	    """
   230	    Keep the half-enclosed chamber hollow and shoot a wide dashed beam through its opening.
   231	
   232	    Input structure:
   233	    - The background is the most common color, and the most frequent non-background color forms a single wall component with one open side.
   234	    - A nearby non-wall color marks the source seed inside the chamber; any remaining non-background pixels are fixed obstacles.
   235	
   236	    Rule:
   237	    - Do not flood-fill the chamber. Instead, use the wall endpoints to infer the outward opening direction and launch a beam of the seed color straight along that axis.
   238	    - The beam is always 3 pixels wide, aligned to the opening's midpoint, colors every other step to form a dashed trail, and each lane stops independently when it hits a wall or obstacle.
   239	
   240	    Key insight:
   241	    - The solver must fuse three visible cues at once: the chamber stays hollow, the emitted trail is a 3-cell-thick stripe rather than a region fill, and that stripe follows a one-on/one-off dash rhythm along the opening direction.
